 Database Schema

Database name: pizzahut

Table	Columns	Description
orders	order_id, date, time	One row per order with its date and time
order_details	order_details_id, order_id, pizza_id, quantity	Line items in each order
pizzas	pizza_id, pizza_type_id, size, price	Each pizza with its size and price
pizza_types	pizza_type_id, name, category, ingredients	Pizza names, categories, and ingredients

Relationships

orders (order_id) ──< order_details (order_id)
order_details (pizza_id) >── pizzas (pizza_id)
pizzas (pizza_type_id) >── pizza_types (pizza_type_id)
 Business Questions & Solutions


1. Total number of orders placed
sql
select count(order_id) as [total_order] from orders;

Result: 21,350 orders

2. Total revenue generated from pizza sales
sql
select
    sum(order_details.quantity * pizzas.price) as total_sales
from order_details
join pizzas on pizzas.pizza_id = order_details.pizza_id;

Result: ≈ 817,860.05

3. Highest-priced pizza
sql
select top 1
    pizza_types.name, pizzas.price
from pizza_types
join pizzas on pizza_types.pizza_type_id = pizzas.pizza_type_id
order by pizzas.price desc;

Result: The Greek Pizza at 35.95

